{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview","id":29987,"title":"Nen (Pantheon Specific Purview)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-14T10:40:47-08:00","id":29987,"title":"Nen (Pantheon Specific Purview)","content":"So I was thinking of PSPs and decided to do one based on the concept of Nen from HunterXHunter. Please post any comments you want, balance and concept-oriented ones would be a bonus, since I might use this in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Nen</span></b><br /> Nen is the life energy produced by all living bodies, it is necessary to life itself. Unaware to most, Nen leaks at a very slow rate away from the body, eventually leading to death when the body is unable to produce as much Nen as it leaks. Scions who delve into the Nen Purview are aware of these facts and are able to control it in their advantage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ten (Nen \u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> The first step into mastering Nen is to learn to keep it from leaking away from the body. Ten is the process of controlling the leak of Nen and having it flowing through and around the body rather than away from it. Since the life energy no longer flows away from the body, aging acts much slower and Scions look younger than they really are.<br /> In addition, when rolling to determine if the Scion is fatebound to another being, halve the number of successes rolled rounded up, due to the flow of legend being much closer to the Scion's body than it normally would.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Zetsu (Nen \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> (Legend Rating) legend per scene<br /> While Ten allows the user to keep Nen from leaking away from the body, Zetsu stops the flow of Nen altogether. Since the user is no longer surrounded by his own Nen, he becomes more sensitive to others Nen, while keeping others from noticing his. However, since Zetsu involves shutting off one's Nen flow, it can be dangerous to leave the body unprotected against any attack.<br /> By paying an amount of legend equal to the Scion's Legend Rating, the Scion cannot become fatebound to another being and counts as if he has no Legend rating until the end of the scene, making it impossible to use Boons, Epics, Knacks and all other powers that a normal human would not have. In addition, Zetsu can be extended to the following scenes, at the cost of 1 legend for each following scene, and can be interrupted at the start of any of the Scion's actions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ren (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 legend per action<br /> Ren is a direct application of Ten, where the user releases a high amount of Nen and keeps it close to the body without leaking. This increases the user's physical strength and durability while increasing the amount of Nen available to be used.<br /> For a number of actions equal to the amount of legend spent, the Scion adds (Nen Rating) to all physical attributes and gains an additional (Nen Rating) temporary legend points. Ren also affects all the derived values from the physical attributes, such as DVs, Feats of Strength, Movement ratings and Soaks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Hatsu (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 willpower + cost of other Boon and Knacks<br /> Hatsu is the release of one's Nen, as to be projected to carry out a certain function. In essence, Hatsu is one's personal expression of Nen that create special and unique skills that reflect one's character.<br /> When the Scion purchases Hatsu, he must choose (Nen Rating) Boons or Knacks; adding new ones to this list as the Scion increases his Nen Rating. The Scion can activate any number of powers within Hatsu or any Nen Boons he knows simultaneously by paying 1 willpower plus the cost of all powers the Scion chooses to activate. Powers used in this manner appear to be formed from one's Nen, before reforming into their original form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Shu (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 legend per action<br /> Shu is an advanced application of Ten that allows users to extend their Nen to envelop an object, allowing them to use that object as if it was an extension of their own body.<br /> The Scion is able to enhance an object he touches for a number of actions equal to the amount of legend spent. The enhanced object becomes indestructible and is able to deal lethal damage at its wielder will. This turns a pack of meaningless cards into many powerful throwing weapons. Armors enhanced this way cannot be destroyed or damaged, but soak the same amount of damage as they previously did.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>In (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 willpower<br /> In is an advanced form of Zetsu used to almost completely conceal one's presence. While in In state, the user becomes almost invisible to those who rely on supernatural methods to find him.<br /> When the Scion activates Zetsu, he can pay an extra 1 willpower to add in In. If he does so he cannot be detected by any supernatural means, such as Boons, Knacks and the dice pool to detect the Scion using In cannot receive bonus dice or successes of any type.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ken (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Legend + Nen<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1+ legend<br /> Ken is an advanced version of the basic Ren technique, where the user maintains a state of Ren over the entire body allowing them to defend against attacks from any direction. While it is useful as a defensive position, Ken becomes tiring of maintaining.<br /> The Scion increases his Bashing and Lethal Soak by an amount equal to the amount of legend spent, against a number of attacks equal to the amount of rolled successes gathered on a roll of (Legend + Nen).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ko (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 legend per success<br /> Ko is an advanced application of Ren and Zetsu by which one concentrates a larger than normal amount of Nen into a specific body part. Ko increases the strength of that one body part, but leaves the rest of the body vulnerable to a counter offensive.<br /> The Scion can enhance any action he performs, adding an amount of successes equal to the amount of legend spent to the dice pool for that action, while giving the user a DV penalty equal to half of the amount of legend spent. This action cannot involve weapons or tools that aren't Relics or indestructible.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>En (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Legend + Nen<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 legend per action<br /> En is an advanced application of Ren and Ten, where one extends his Nen further than normal while keeping it together and without leaking. Someone using En can feel the shape and movement of anything entering his Nen field, with the downside of being very tiring.<br /> The Scion using En becomes fully aware of anything moving within a number of miles equal to the number of successes gathered on a roll of (Legend + Nen), lasting for a number of actions equal to the amount of legend spent.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ryu (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 legend per success<br /> Ryu is the term for the real time application of Ko, rapidly moving the Nen to enhance specific parts of one's body.<br /> For a number of actions equal to the Scion's Nen rating, he is able to add an amount of successes to any action he performs or to his Bashing and Lethal Soak equal to the amount of legend spent. These can only be set at the start of the Scion's action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Opinions?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Version 1:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ten (Nen \u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> The first step into mastering Nen is to learn to keep it from leaking away from the body. Ten is the process of controlling the leak of Nen and having it flowing through and around the body rather than away from it. Since the life energy no longer flows away from the body, aging acts much slower and Scions