tion + Nen), lasting for a number of actions equal to the amount of legend spent.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ryu (Nen \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 legend per success<br /> Ryu is the term for the real time application of Ko, rapidly moving the Nen to enhance specific parts of one's body.<br /> For a number of actions equal to the Scion's Nen rating, he is able to add an amount of successes to any action he performs or to his Bashing and Lethal Soak equal to the amount of legend spent. These can only be set at the start of the Scion's action.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":".  Update 12-21-2013, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T08:04:00-08:00","id":30423,"title":"","content":"First off - What pantheon is this specific to?<br /> <br /> TEN: Pretty cool, chock full of flavor.<br /> ZETSU: Is fatebinding such a problem that you would spend points to become mortal? This is remarkably dangerous for very little payoff.<br /> REN: Holy crap. Apparently all the awesome was drained from ZETSU and added to REN (note - this is not overpowered). Place a &quot;once per scene&quot; in there and call it soup.<br /> HATSU: Standard re-skinning of Riastrad (not sure of spelling).<br /> SHU: Interesting - like a better &quot;Titanium Tools&quot;. I almost want some sort of limiter on this (once per scene per object, object takes NEN damage once finished), but it is a 5-dot Boon. Any thought of allowing a boost in Soak (building armor with this, not just weapons)?<br /> IN: It might be good, but my dislike of ZETSU rubs off on this one.<br /> KEN: As a 2 or 3-dot Boon, this would be cool. As a 7-dot boon? I would at least expect some amount of Aggravated soak boost.<br /> KO: I like the idea, but it is seriously flawed. The reduced DV is meaningless when used with out-of-combat actions. Also, can I use this for hacking with a relic computer? What about research with a relic card catalog (I have seen this in a game)?<br /> EN: It's a 9-dot Boon. I would boost the legend cost, but have its range be [Legend Rating x 5] yards and last a number of actions (or ticks if the cost is low) equal to successes.<br /> RYU: Honestly, I think it's under-powered. My criticism of KEN still stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T08:41:15-08:00","id":30440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off - What pantheon is this specific to?</div> </div> </div> </div>None yet.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TEN: Pretty cool, chock full of flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ZETSU: Is fatebinding such a problem that you would spend points to become mortal? This is remarkably dangerous for very little payoff.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea for Zetsu is to suppress Nen completely, thus suppressing the Legend of a Scion completely and removing all things that make him legendary.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">REN: Holy crap. Apparently all the awesome was drained from ZETSU and added to REN (note - this is not overpowered). Place a &quot;once per scene&quot; in there and call it soup.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is that strong, when you buy it a +3 to Str is about +1.5 damage when you hit, +3 to Dex is about +2 to DVs and +1.5 successes to hit (both add at most +2 damage) and a +3 to Stamina is only +3 Bashing Soak and +2 Lethal Soak. At Legend 12 is only +10 meaning +8 damage at most and +5 to Dvs. Not much at all, I don't see a need to add it a limit to scenes, it takes a 5 tick action to activate it for X actions and if it runs out you can deploy it again.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HATSU: Standard re-skinning of Riastrad (not sure of spelling).</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit yes, but Hatsu allows you to choose which ones you activate (instead of forcing you to activate all of them) and add all the Nen Boon for free, with no downsides.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SHU: Interesting - like a better &quot;Titanium Tools&quot;. I almost want some sort of limiter on this (once per scene per object, object takes NEN damage once finished), but it is a 5-dot Boon. Any thought of allowing a boost in Soak (building armor with this, not just weapons)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It just transforms an object turning it indestructible. A limiter might be required, but definitely not damage at the end. The idea is to keep the user's Nen with the object, protecting it.<br /> <br /> Regarding its use on armors, I must admit that I hadn't thought about it. Two situations come to mind: A) it increases the armor's hardness to infinite, meaning that the damage still has to go through soak to damage the wearer but the armor itself is indestructible, and B) it increases the armor's soak to infinite, meaning that the wearer is immune to damage during X actions.<br /> The first has little meaning and the second is probably overpowered without the called shots. Not sure what to do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IN: It might be good, but my dislike of ZETSU rubs off on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable, but the idea is to remove oneself throughly from Fate, thus becoming impossible to track with supernatural aid. When one wants to disappear, becoming mortal might be a good thing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KEN: As a 2 or 3-dot Boon, this would be cool. As a 7-dot boon? I would at least expect some amount of Aggravated soak boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aggravated Soak is minimal on Gods, even Epic Stamina 10 only gives 10 Aggravated Soak. The objective isn't to face off the Damage Monster with it for a great deal of time, but to survive enough time to escape or to be able to handle someone a bit stronger than the user.<br /> <br /> Here is an example: At Legend 8, Scion A has bought Ken. Since he has no other powers that enhance his fighting abilities, he uses Hatsu to call Ren and Ken, paying 10 legend each for a total cost of 1 willpower and 20 legend. Ren gives him +7 to Strength (+3.5 Damage), +7 to Dexterity (+3.5 to hit and +4 to DVs) and +7 to Stamina (+0/+4/+7 to Soak) and Ken gives him +0/+10/+10 to Soak, for the next 7 to 10 actions.<br /> It only costs +10 legend than Colossus (War 7), half the power to Strength but adds more to Dexterity and almost the same Soak, while doing so quietly and without becoming a Giant Statue of brass and steel. Also War is much more oriented to dishing out damage.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KO: I like the idea, but it is seriously flawed. The reduced DV is meaningless when used with out-of-combat actions. Also, can I use this for hacking with a relic computer? What about research with a relic card catalog (I have seen this in a game)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the idea, to use it freely out of combat. In combat you have to deal with its consequences.<br /> <br /> Also if used in Hatsu with Ren and Ken, becomes much more powerful.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EN: It's a 9-dot Boon. I would boost the legend cost, but have its range be [Legend Rating x 5] yards and last a number of actions (or ticks if the cost is low) equal to successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The range is indeed a bit low on someone who doesn't have Epic Perception or even with it. I might just say it is (roll Nen) miles or something like that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30423#post30423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RYU: Honestly, I think it's under-powered. My criticism of KEN still stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the best of Ko and Ken, for it circumvents Ko's weakness and adds the flexibility to flip between adding power to hit someone or to block something.<br /> <br /> Nen's idea is to be flexible and not become able to dish out a great amount of damage or soak it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":". 12-15-2013, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T11:10:24-08:00","id":30491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30440#post30440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understandable, but the idea is to remove oneself throughly from Fate, thus becoming impossible to track with supernatural aid. When one wants to disappear, becoming mortal might be a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to comment on the rest of the boons, but I wanted to chime in on this one. While there are a few cases where In might be meaningful, generally Zetsu is not going to last long enough to get any value out of In. A handful of actions will not allow you to get very far without epics and boons, and anyone with moderate mental epics is going to predict your actions because you have become so mentally deficient. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Technically the same is true of Zetsu, but there are a lot more situations where Zetsu might be useful than ones where In might be useful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T11:53:25-08:00","id":30507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30491#post30491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to comment on the rest of the boons, but I wanted to chime in on this one. While there are a few cases where In might be meaningful, generally Zetsu is not going to last long enough to get any value out of In. A handful of actions will not allow you to get very far without epics and boons, and anyone with moderate mental epics is going to predict your actions because you have become so mentally deficient. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Technically the same is true of Zetsu, but there are a lot more situations where Zetsu might be useful than ones where In might be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nop, you can't use Epics to try to find him because it adds bonus successes. That is the whole point of In, you have to try to find him as a normal mortal would.<br /> <br /> Maybe the problem is with Zetsu's duration... what about increasing it to 1 legend per day? Or a bit more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":". 12-15-2013, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T01:46:09-08:00","id":30841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30507#post30507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, you can't use Epics to try to find him because it adds bonus successes. That is the whole point of In, you have to try to find him as a normal mortal would.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not suggesting they use their epics to try and actively detect where he is now, but to use their epics to try and anticipate where he will be later. It's the difference between external detection and internal deduction (like the difference between being unable to see because of too much darkness, and being unable to see because you lack eyes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30507#post30507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the problem is with Zetsu's duration... what about increasing it to 1 legend per day? Or a bit more?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Legend per day might work, but I prefer scene long durations. Some scenes take several days, but often you end up fitting several scenes into a single day. Maybe something along the lines of 3 Legend and 1 Willpower per scene?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T10:49:39-08:00","id":31066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30841#post30841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not suggesting they use their epics to try and actively detect where he is now, but to use their epics to try and anticipate where he will be later. It's the difference between external detection and internal deduction (like the difference between being unable to see because of too much darkness, and being unable to see because you lack eyes).</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you are trying to say. I wonder if I should even allow that, since In is about removing oneself entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/29987-nen-pantheon-specific-purview?p=30841#post30841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Legend per day might work, but I prefer scene long durations. Some scenes take several days, but often you end up fitting several scenes into a single day. Maybe something along the lines of 3 Legend and 1 Willpower per scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Zetsu and In probably is balanced,but not just for Zetsu, which already carries a large penalty. 3 legend per Scene for Zetsu and 1 willpower for In works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:34:54-08:00","id":31126,"title":"","content":"Let me praise you for a really unique PSP. This has flavor and it isn't a flavor we've seen before. Hip, Hip, Hooray!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T13:49:41-08:00","id":34592,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to say that I updated the Purview slightly considering the feedback. Soon, I'll post a thread with a fictitious Pantheon that uses it. EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/34636-the-occuria-ficticious-pantheon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...cious-pantheon</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":". 12-21-2013, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}